# Git

- Start every new branch off `main`.
- Prefix branches with `feat/`, `test/`, or `bugfix/` (never `cursor/`).
- Ask before pushing.
- Put a summary in the commit message.
- When changing existing code, scan repo dependencies so modules stay compatible.

# Layout

- Source in `src/`.
- Tests in `test/`.
- Hunt sim lives in `src/simulation/` so hardware code can share this repo.

# Size and style

- Keep functions under 45 lines.
- Use tabs for indentation.
- Write concise code.
- Comment why a change exists, not only what it does.
- Do not erase old comments that are still useful.

# Web

- After UI/layout/state changes, verify in the browser end to end (click, type, navigate). A screenshot is not enough.
